messages.content:
You are assisting with business process modelling. A legal rule has been confirmed to apply to the business process described below. Write, in plain language, what the rule requires at one step of the process.

INSTRUCTIONS
- requirement: one or two short, plain sentences, at most 40 words in total, that say what is required at the process step below and whether it is required before, at or after that step.
- State what is required as a fact about the process (for example "the customer is told ..."). Do not give instructions about a process model or diagram, such as adding, drawing or modelling a task.
- Use your own plain words. Do not copy the legal text: at most a few words in a row may be the same as in the legal passage.
- Name the people and departments as the process description names them. Do not use the words "shall", "controller", "data subject" or "processor".
- Keep every trigger and condition the obligation states, for example "on request", "where applicable" or "if the customer asks". The requirement must not apply in more situations than the obligation does.
- Use only what the obligation says. Do not add any obligation, actor, deadline, condition, document or step that is not in it, and do not combine it with other rules or with general knowledge.
- step_quote: copy, exactly and word for word, the words of the process description that name the step where the requirement applies. It is checked automatically.
- triggers: one entry for every trigger or condition the obligation states. "trigger": its words copied exactly from the OBLIGATION; "kept_as": the words of your requirement, copied exactly, that keep it. Both are checked automatically. Use an empty list if the obligation states none.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE (made up, for the format only)
Obligation: "the supplier shall, at the purchaser's request, inform the purchaser in writing of the expected date of each instalment before the first delivery"
Process step: the warehouse ships the order ("The warehouse ships the order in several parcels")
Answer: {"requirement": "If the customer asks, the customer is told in writing, before the warehouse ships the first parcel, when each parcel will arrive.", "step_quote": "The warehouse ships the order in several parcels", "triggers": [{"trigger": "at the purchaser's request", "kept_as": "If the customer asks"}, {"trigger": "before the first delivery", "kept_as": "before the warehouse ships the first parcel"}]}

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "TriggerKept": {
      "properties": {
        "trigger": {
          "description": "A trigger or condition of the obligation, copied exactly from the OBLIGATION",
          "title": "Trigger",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kept_as": {
          "description": "The words of the requirement, copied exactly, that keep this trigger",
          "title": "Kept As",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "trigger",
        "kept_as"
      ],
      "title": "TriggerKept",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "requirement": {
      "description": "One or two sentences: what the rule requires, tied to the process step",
      "title": "Requirement",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "step_quote": {
      "description": "Exact words copied from the process description that name the step",
      "title": "Step Quote",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "triggers": {
      "description": "Every trigger or condition the obligation states; empty list if none",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/TriggerKept"
      },
      "title": "Triggers",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "requirement",
    "step_quote",
    "triggers"
  ],
  "title": "RequirementOutputV2",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
This process begins when a potential customer inquires about a product or service.
Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions.
If the customer is interested, they are guided through selecting the appropriate product or service.
Next, the sales representative provides a quote, and after approval from the customer, the process moves to order placement.
The order is then recorded in the system, and the customer receives confirmation of their order.
The process ends when the order is successfully placed and confirmed.

LEGAL PASSAGE
[GDPR-Art13-1] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
1. Where personal data relating to a data subject are collected from the data subject, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information:
(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative;
(b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable;
(c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing;
(d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party;
(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any;
(f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means by which to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.

OBLIGATION
the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with all of the following information: (a) the identity and the contact details of the controller and, where applicable, of the controller's representative; (b) the contact details of the data protection officer, where applicable; (c) the purposes of the processing for which the personal data are intended as well as the legal basis for the processing; (d) where the processing is based on point (f) of Article 6(1), the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party; (e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data, if any; (f) where applicable, the fact that the controller intends to transfer personal data to a third country or international organisation and the existence or absence of an adequacy decision by the Commission, or in the case of transfers referred to in Article 46 or 47, or the second subparagraph of Article 49(1), reference to the appropriate or suitable safeguards and the means by which to obtain a copy of them or where they have been made available.

PROCESS STEP
Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions ("Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions")

